  <footer class="provenance">
    <h2 class="prov-h">Sources, method and revisions</h2>
    <div class="cols">
      <div>
        <h6>Source of record</h6>
        <p>Ministry of Statistics &amp; Programme Implementation, National Statistical Office, Periodic Labour Force Survey, retrieved through the eSankhyiki API, vintage <b id="prov-vintage" set:html={TX["prov-vintage"]}></b>. Every indicator MoSPI serves (participation, worker and unemployment rates; the distribution of workers by status, industry, occupation and enterprise; regular employees' job conditions; regular wages, casual wages and self-employment earnings) is fetched whole, at every cut, and archived as served before any bundle is cut from it.</p>
        <p>Two survey designs. The original design: annual reports on agriculture years 2017-18 to 2023-24, calendar-year estimates {cyOldYears[0]} to {cyOldYears.at(-1)}, and the urban quarterly bulletin to {qLabel(qDates.at(-1))}. The revamped design, from January 2025: the monthly bulletin ({PM.long}), the quarterly bulletin with villages and 22 states ({qn(q25First)} to {qn(q25Last)}), and calendar-year estimates from {cyYear}. Never spliced. Dadra &amp; Nagar Haveli and Daman &amp; Diu report separately to 2019-20 and as one merged UT thereafter.</p>
        <p>Withheld, every case disclosed on its series and kept in the raw archive: values the data service garbles ("l0.8", "IS.2", a worker ratio of 415); cells whose three ratios contradict each other (Apr–Jun 2019 urban unemployment is carried as 21.6 where the bulletin says 8.9); cells with no sampled person; the state tables of Apr–Jun 2025 and the participation table of Jul–Sep 2025 from Jammu &amp; Kashmir on, whose state labels the service shifted one row (checked against the bulletin); and the 2017-18 rural-plus-urban earnings aggregates for regular and self-employed workers, whose implied urban weight contradicts every later year. Jan–Mar 2025 was never published in the quarterly bulletin. The calendar-year job-contract tables are served with their category label missing and cannot be used; the agriculture-year ones are drawn in §08.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>Revisions &amp; uncertainty</h6>
        <p>PLFS figures are final on release. The monthly bulletin (from April 2025) and the quarterly bulletin (urban, from 2018) are separate instruments with separate coverage: shown side by side, never joined.</p>
        <p>Where something is not measured, this guide says "we do not know" rather than inventing a number.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h6>This guide</h6>
        <p>Labour, version 1.4, reads the whole PLFS: both survey designs side by side (§03, §04), the quarterly bulletin's villages and states, young people, work and pay in every state, women's work by social group and religion, and regular employees' job conditions. Next scheduled revision: on release of the next monthly bulletin.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="fine">
      <span>India Atlas, PLFS</span>
      <span>Vintage <span id="prov-vintage2" set:html={TX["prov-vintage2"]}></span>, CWS and PS+SS, never spliced</span>
      <span>Set in Source Serif 4 and Golos Text</span>
    </div>
  </footer>

